{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_bdrk_mksjlpymrxmwy4m5sk5cokq7x5yamhlhya25vy3tvjmf5nsfeeuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete and fully verified. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the SPHINCS+ reference C project in `c_src/` to pure Rust in `translation/`, producing **byte-identical output** to the C binary across **all 48 build configurations** (verified against golden outputs generated from the compiled C reference).\n\n### Architecture\n- **Build-time configurability preserved via Cargo features** — each CMake cache variable value became a lowercase feature: backends (`haraka`, `sha2`, `shake`, `blake`), thash variants (`robust`, `simple`), and security levels (`128s/f`, `192s/f`, `256s/f`). Defaults match CMake (`haraka`, `robust`, `128s`).\n- **`build.rs`** resolves features into a single active selection (`spx_backend`/`spx_thash`/`spx_secpar`/`spx_sha512`/`spx_blake512` cfgs) with priority + fallback, so **every feature combination compiles** (verified: empty, all-at-once, and conflicting sets).\n- Produces **both** `libsphincs_plus.so` (cdylib) and the `driver` binary.\n\n### Faithful translation details\n- Every `.c` file has a complete Rust equivalent (29 source modules); no stubs.\n- All public C functions are `#[no_mangle]`/`#[export_name]` `extern \"C\"` with exact C signatures and correct final linker symbol names, including the `SPX_`-namespaced ones (`SPX_thash`, `SPX_prf_addr`, …) and plain names (`crypto_sign_*`, `randombytes`, `sha256`, `shake256`, `blake512`, …).\n- No OpenSSL — implemented pure-Rust AES-256 for the CTR-DRBG (network to crates.io was blocked, so zero external dependencies).\n- Reproduced C quirks exactly (e.g., BLAKE `update` called with byte counts as bit-lengths; `SPX_BLAKE512` selecting BLAKE-512 for multi-block thash at 192/256; the sk_seed-not-hashed detail in BLAKE `prf_addr`).\n\n### Key debugging win\nWhen BLAKE 192/256 initially mismatched, I isolated it via C-vs-Rust component tests down to a missed `#define SPX_BLAKE512 1` in the 192/256 param headers, then added the BLAKE-512 multi-block thash path — after which all configs matched.\n\n`c_src/` was never modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":481894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"562c112f-521a-4b18-b7fd-2e147d3d0f73","uuid":"bab193a9-f948-4c94-b00e-7482d84348cb","timestamp":"2026-08-28T23:41:05.313Z"}
